IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`
IMPORT `ea-retrenchment-reporting-notification`

-- Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019 (S 200/2019), made
-- under s 96A(1) of the Employment Act 1968 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the
-- law. Day numbers count from day 0 = Monday 1 November 2021, so day 1806 is
-- Monday 12 October 2026 (1 November 2021 to 1 November 2026 is 5 x 365 + 1
-- (29 February 2024) = 1826 days; less 20 = 1806). Public holidays are not in
-- the deposit: every holiday used below is ILLUSTRATIVE, not a claim that the
-- day was or will be a public holiday.

GIVEN `under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `end date` IS A BOOLEAN, `months` IS A NUMBER
    , `workforce` IS A NUMBER
    , `employer's initiative` IS A BOOLEAN, `redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `given on` IS A NUMBER, `takes effect on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice of retrenchment`
DECIDE `a notice` `under the Act` `end date` `months` `workforce` `employer's initiative` `redundancy` `given on` `takes effect on` IS
    `Notice of retrenchment` WITH
        `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act` IS `under the Act`
        `the contract` IS `Contract of service` WITH
            `specifies an end date` IS `end date`
            `term of employment in months` IS `months`
        `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS `workforce`
        `the employer initiated the termination` IS `employer's initiative`
        `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation` IS `redundancy`
        `the day the notice is given` IS `given on`
        `the day the notice takes effect` IS `takes effect on`

GIVEN `differs` IS A BOOLEAN, `union` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Schedule circumstances`
DECIDE `circumstances` `differs` `union` `paid` IS
    `Schedule circumstances` WITH
        `the trade name differs from the name` IS `differs`
        `the employer recognises a trade union` IS `union`
        `retrenchment benefits were paid to the employee` IS `paid`

§ `REQ-0289 (Haziq scenario, event h065)`

-- 40 employees, all on contracts with no end date (assumed), 12 retrenched for
-- redundancy, notices given on Monday 12 October 2026 (day 1806, illustrative),
-- taking effect a month later. Must it notify? Yes: each of the 12 notices
-- needs a retrenchment report (para 3(1)).
#ASSERT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE FALSE 0 40 TRUE TRUE 1806 1837)
#ASSERT `is an employer within the Notification` 40
-- Through s 96A(2): the Notification applies, so the duty is owed.
#ASSERT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` 40 12 0)
-- Within what time? Not later than 5 working days after the day of the notice
-- (para 4). With no public holiday in the week: Tue 13 (1), Wed 14 (2),
-- Thu 15 (3), Fri 16 (4), skip Sat 17 and Sun 18, Mon 19 October (5) = day 1813.
#ASSERT `the number of working days allowed` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the last day for the retrenchment report` 1806 EMPTY EQUALS 1813
-- In what form? The Ministry of Manpower website form, unless the Commissioner
-- allows otherwise (para 5).
#ASSERT `the report is in the required form` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the report is in the required form` FALSE FALSE
-- With what particulars? Schedule para 1 about the employer (5 where the trade
-- name is the same and no union is recognised) and Schedule para 2 about each
-- of the 12 (7 each where retrenchment benefits were paid).
#ASSERT `the number of employer particulars required` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the number of particulars required for each retrenched employee` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 7
-- None of the 12 reported: 12 occasions for a contravention notice (s 126B(1)(aa)).
#ASSERT `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` 40 12 0) EQUALS 12

§ `Paragraph 3(1) -- no minimum number retrenched`

-- The ledger expected "5 or more within 6 months". The deposited text has no
-- such line: one notice to one covered employee, by a 10-employee employer, is enough.
#ASSERT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE FALSE 0 10 TRUE TRUE 1806 1837)
#ASSERT `the employer must furnish retrenchment information to the Commissioner` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` 10 1 0)
-- A 9-employee employer is not an "employer" for the Notification.
#ASSERT NOT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE FALSE 0 9 TRUE TRUE 1806 1837)
-- When the notice takes effect does not matter (para 3(1), para 2(3)).
#ASSERT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE FALSE 0 40 TRUE TRUE 1806 2200)
-- A notice given on Sunday 31 October 2021 (day -1) is outside the current para 3(1).
#ASSERT NOT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE FALSE 0 40 TRUE TRUE (0 MINUS 1) 30)

§ `Paragraph 2(2) -- which employees`

#ASSERT `the contract brings the employee within the Notification` (`Contract of service` WITH `specifies an end date` IS FALSE, `term of employment in months` IS 0)
#ASSERT `the contract brings the employee within the Notification` (`Contract of service` WITH `specifies an end date` IS TRUE, `term of employment in months` IS 6)
#ASSERT NOT `the contract brings the employee within the Notification` (`Contract of service` WITH `specifies an end date` IS TRUE, `term of employment in months` IS 5)
-- A 3-month fixed-term employee let go for redundancy: no report.
#ASSERT NOT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE TRUE 3 40 TRUE TRUE 1806 1837)
-- A domestic worker is not an "employee" under s 2(1) of the Act: no report.
#ASSERT NOT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` FALSE FALSE 0 40 TRUE TRUE 1806 1837)

§ `Paragraph 2(1) -- "retrench"`

#ASSERT `is a retrenchment within the Notification` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `is a retrenchment within the Notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Not at the employer's initiative (e.g. a resignation): no report.
#ASSERT NOT `a retrenchment report must be given for the notice` (`a notice` TRUE FALSE 0 40 FALSE TRUE 1806 1837)

§ `Paragraphs 2(1) and 4 -- working days and the deadline`

-- Day 0 is a Monday; day 5 is Saturday 6 November 2021.
#ASSERT `the weekday of day` 1806 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `is a working day` 4 EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` 5 EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` 3 (LIST 3)
-- Notice on Monday 1 November 2021: days 1, 2, 3, 4, then Monday day 7.
#ASSERT `the last day for the retrenchment report` 0 EMPTY EQUALS 7
-- Treating day 3 as a public holiday (illustrative): 1, 2, 4, 7, 8.
#ASSERT `the last day for the retrenchment report` 0 (LIST 3) EQUALS 8
-- Notice on Friday 16 October 2026 (1810): Mon 1813, 1814, 1815, 1816, Fri 1817.
#ASSERT `the last day for the retrenchment report` 1810 EMPTY EQUALS 1817
-- Notice on Saturday 17 October 2026 (1811): the same five working days.
#ASSERT `the last day for the retrenchment report` 1811 EMPTY EQUALS 1817
-- Haziq week with Wednesday 14 October (1808) treated as a holiday: 1807, 1809,
-- 1810, 1813, 1814.
#ASSERT `the last day for the retrenchment report` 1806 (LIST 1808) EQUALS 1814
#ASSERT `the report is given in time` 1806 1813 EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `the report is given in time` 1806 1814 EMPTY
#ASSERT `the report is given in time` 1806 1814 (LIST 1808)

§ `The Schedule -- which particulars`

#ASSERT `the particular is required` `the employer's name and address` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is required` `the employer's trade name` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the particular is required` `the employer's trade name` (`circumstances` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is required` `the reasons no retrenchment benefits were paid` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the particular is required` `the reasons no retrenchment benefits were paid` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the particular is about the employer` `the employer's workforce on the notice date by citizenship`
-- A different trade name and a recognised union: all 7 employer particulars.
#ASSERT `the number of employer particulars required` (`circumstances` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 7
-- No retrenchment benefit paid: 8 particulars for that employee, reasons included.
#ASSERT `the number of particulars required for each retrenched employee` (`circumstances` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 8

§ `Section 96A(2) and s 126B(1)(aa) on the Notification's facts`

-- 9 of 12 reported properly: not complied; 3 occasions (12 - 9 = 3).
#ASSERT NOT `the employer has complied with section 96A(2)` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` 40 12 9)
#ASSERT `the occasions a contravention notice may cover under section 126B(1)(aa)` (`the section 96A facts under the 2019 Notification` 40 12 9) EQUALS 3
